From 6081861cde729bc36f2be0b0719cf5ee780934c2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arnaldo Lima <arnaldolimaof@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 00:47:35 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] SPU float fast path in the SPU's own MXCSR mode;
 SPURS_MAXCONT

- spu_run_with_halt puts the thread in round-toward-zero + FTZ + DAZ while
  SPU code runs (SPU_FAST_FP=0: off). That is single-precision SPU
  arithmetic, so fa/fs/fm are one SSE op when no lane can leave the normal
  range (extended range and possible overflow take the exact path). fma
  uses the double path without TwoSum there: the double sum truncates, and
  truncating it again to 24 bits is the SPU's one truncation. The scalar
  fix-ups and SPU double precision (dfa/dfs/dfm/dfma family, frds, double
  compares) switch back to the standard mode for their span.
- test_spu_float_neon --spu-mode: every check again in that mode; bit for
  bit against the references (8M cases) in both.
- -frounding-math (clang-cl: /clang:) for the runtime's C sources and lifted
  SPU code, so the compiler does not fold float ops on constants under
  round-to-nearest.
- SPURS_MAXCONT=<wid>=<n>: more SPUs on a workload than the title asked for
  (diagnostic; Ascension's menu list does not gain from it).

Ascension's main menu: module 0be5cb89a80c 760 -> 690 ms/s.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
